Commit 7e59e1f0 changes audit-gate.mjs in three places.
`coveringEntry` at lines 189-199 now binds both identity fields.
An id-keyed entry must hold the same id and the same package.
A pkg-keyed entry must hold the same package.
Any other case returns null, so `decide` at lines 211-238 pushes a FAIL.
`isCalendarDate` at lines 108-118 rejects impossible dates such as 2026-02-31.
`checkEntry` at lines 151-153 reports that failure.

## Security effect of the change

Input handling is unchanged.
Line 36 and lines 367-368 still spawn npm with an array argument list and no shell.
Line 416 still builds the snapshot path from the fixed folder, a validated key and an ISO stamp.
The diff has no hunk in that region.

Fail-closed behavior is stronger, not weaker.
`isRecord` at lines 96-101 rejects null, functions and arrays.
A prototype key such as __proto__ or constructor cannot pass the identity checks.
A network or JSON failure still exits non-zero.

The three sharp entries pass the stricter rule with unchanged data.
Each entry id equals the advisory id and each package is sharp.
The date 2026-12-15 is a real calendar date.

One residual stays with no current exposure.
A pkg-keyed entry still covers every advisory of that package at the entry severity.
Lines 296-298 treat that as intended behavior.
The current allowlist holds no pkg-keyed entry.

